{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/541-dream-deprogramming","id":541,"title":"Dream Deprogramming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-01T14:50:18-07:00","id":541,"title":"Dream Deprogramming","content":"<b>Dream Deprogramming </b><br /> <br /> Changelings can use dreams for a lot of things. They can teach, heal and they can even break the unnatural hold a supernatural power keeps over the mind. This is a three stage process. First the Changeling must enter or craft a Dream appropriate to the influence they wish to remove. A dark Transylvanian landscape under the watchful gaze of a thunder-lit castle might work for a Vampire's mental domination, but not for a Flowering Fariest's use of Fleeting Spring.<br /> <br /> The second stage is the simplest, once inside the Dream the Changeling must spend a point of Glamour to forge the connection between the Dream and the supernatural power. This summons the Dream Tyrant and leads to the third stage. The Changeling must defeat the Dream Tyrant in Oneiromachical combat to free the dreamer.<br /> <br /> <b>Sidebar: Freeing yourself. </b><br /> <i>The crude mental tricks performed by Changelings and sorcerers are nothing compared to what a Changeling experienced in Arcadia. After overcoming the Gentry's mental manipulations Changelings can often notice when they're affected by mental techniques.<br /> <br /> While under the effects of mind affecting magic a Changeling with a Clarity of 5 or more can roll Clarity every time they fall asleep. On a success they enter a Dream and proceed directly to the third stage. There is no need to spend Glamour when the mind is already fighting the intrusion.<br /> <br /> Merit: Second Thoughts (OOO)<br /> Perquisite: Non-Changeling, Composure 3, Lucid Dreamer.<br /> <br /> Although only Changelings have the mastery of Dreams to enter a mind and unpick the supernatural control. It doesn\u2019t require Glamour when a mind is able to defend itself. The Merit Second Thoughts works like using Clarity to free yourself, but roll Composure instead.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Dream Tyrants</b><br /> Changelings give the name Dream Tyrants to the Dream representation of supernatural mental influence. Within a Dream they appear any other character and may be talked too, fought and even vanquished.<br /> <br /> To Create a Dream Tyrant start with one in every attribute. Distribute a number of dots among Power Attributes equal to the number of successes rolled when extending mental dominion over the dreamer. Distribute a number of dots among Finesse Attributes equal to the creators score in Dominate, Mind, Vainglory or equivalents. Changelings may use Mantle for Court Contracts. Finally distribute a number of dots equal to the influencer's Wyrd, Blood Potency or equivalent among Resistance attributes. Finally the Oneiromancy Skill is the skill used to activate the power, the Dream Tyrant has it at the same level as it's creator. Oneiromachy benefits from concentrating on single attributes and the Storyteller should feel free to do so. Magical spells are not noted for their well rounded personalities.<br /> <br /> <b>Dream Henchmen</b><br /> People who find themselves in opposition to Changelings sometimes armour their spells against pesky dreamcrafters. Once someone has exerted unnatural influence upon another they may use a second power, such as Mind magic or a Dominate Devotion, to create Dream Henchmen. Changelings use Dreamscaping to reinforce the effects of their Contracts. Each Dream Tyrant may have a number of Henchmen equal to it's creator's Wyrd or equivalent.<br /> <br /> Build Dream Henchmen like Dream Tyrants but assign dots from Successes to any attribute. It is not necessary to defeat a Dream Henchman, but they are sure to do everything in their power to protect the Dream Tyrant.<br /> <br /> <b>Corrupted Incubi</b><br /> The most perverse magics can rewrite, or replace an entire personality. When this happens the Changeling attempting to free the origonal mind might uncover Corrupted Incubi, part of the mind's own defences that now regard the Dream Tyrant as belonging here, and the Changeling as the invader acting against a rightful part of the mind.<br /> <br /> Changelings have reported seeing full blown civil wars between the Corrupted Incubi and uncorrupted Incubi or small pockets uncorrupted Incubi fighting a rebellion against a mind under total thrall.<br /> <br /> Destroying the Dream Tyrant does not nessacarially purify all Incubi of corruption, they may linger on as scars of such horrific mental abuse. But without the Dream Tyrant the healing process can begin.<br /> <br /> Build Corrupted Incubi as normal dream residents.<br /> <br /> Sidebar: Bastions and Mind Control.<br /> If a Changeling with the Bastion Merit can get just the merest moment of sleep they can resist mind control, for a while anyway, by entering their Bastion and refusing to wake up. The spell takes effect like normal and creates a Dream Tyrant. But the Tyrant must assault and overcome the Bastion before it can take over the body. If this lasts long enough other members of the Motley may join the fight, or just drop by the Bastion for a night to learn the location of their trapped comrade\u2019s body so they can mount a rescue.<br /> <br /> A skilled Oneiromacher may protect his body from control for an extended period. Destroying attacking Dream Tyrants before they can breach the walls. Much to the confusion of their captor who simply sees an abnormally tough mind resist spell after spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T16:17:56-07:00","id":643,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I don't believe I've seen this work of yours before.<br /> <br /> Since it opens more stories, what would a Dream Tyrant of the Vinculum be like, in your opinion? Besides very scary, since it's a combination of drug addiction, supernaturally-induced love and loyalty, and the raw power of the Beast? And what fun effects (for the vampire, a changeling who pulls it off deserves to have a break, however small given the fact that there is now a ghoul who is very pissed off at their former master and likely wants their help repaying their abuses in full) will destroying it have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T16:33:33-07:00","id":671,"title":"","content":"Do you read Erfworld? <a href=\"http://Do you read Erfworld? This page might be help\" target=\"_blank\">This page</a> might be helpful. (Major spoilers though).<br /> <br /> <br /> I would say that the Dream Tyrant of the Vinculum would look like whatever or whoever the poor sap loved before the Vampire got to him; but clearly corrupted. I'd throw in a lot of corrupted incubi too, since the Vinculum spreads everywhere and causes trouble. I'd probably set the scene with lots of vein/vine hybrids that grow through everything to again represent how the Vinculum seeps into everywhere rather than sits in one place like a dominate command.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.the